From: opencode agent <opencode-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 39/39] Do not call nl_langinfo() on Android

nl_langinfo() is only available from API 26 on Android, so it is not
declared when the JDK is built for API 24.  The same fix as the one the
Termux package uses for the other two places that call it.

---
--- a/src/java.base/unix/native/libjava/java_props_md.c
+++ b/src/java.base/unix/native/libjava/java_props_md.c
@@ -287,8 +287,15 @@
          * Euro locales, in particular. */
         if (strcmp(p, "ISO8859-15") == 0)
             p = "ISO8859-15";
+#ifdef __ANDROID__
+        /* nl_langinfo() is only available from API 26 on Android and the
+         * locale support of Android is rudimentary anyway. */
+        else
+            p = "UTF-8";
+#else
         else
             p = nl_langinfo(CODESET);
+#endif
 
         /* Convert the bare "646" used on Solaris to a proper IANA name */
         if (strcmp(p, "646") == 0)
